#!/bin/sh
# saguaro-tools — network diagnostics adapter (ping/DNS/traceroute/mtr/http),
# optionally bound to a chosen interface. Read-only probes, allow-listed only;
# every argument is charset-validated and each run is time-bounded.
#
#   ping  HOST [IFACE]
#   dns   HOST [SERVER]
#   trace HOST [IFACE]
#   mtr   HOST [IFACE]
#   http  HOST [IFACE]
set -eu

[ "$(id -u)" = 0 ] || { echo "must run as root (via sudo)" >&2; exit 1; }

valid_host()  { echo "$1" | grep -Eq '^[A-Za-z0-9]([A-Za-z0-9.-]{0,252})$'; }
valid_iface() { echo "$1" | grep -Eq '^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,15}$' && [ -e "/sys/class/net/$1" ]; }
valid_ip()    { echo "$1" | grep -Eq '^([0-9]{1,3}\.){3}[0-9]{1,3}$'; }

# capture is dispatched here, before the generic host check below, because it has
# its own positional args (IFACE COUNT PROTO HOST PORT) and no mandatory host.
# Every value is charset-validated; the tcpdump FILTER is assembled from those
# validated tokens as SEPARATE argv words (never an eval'd shell string), and the
# run is header-only (-s 96), non-promiscuous (-p), packet-capped (-c) and
# time-bounded (timeout). No -w/-z/-G so there is no file write or post-command.
if [ "${1:-}" = capture ]; then
  IFACE="${2:-}"; COUNT="${3:-}"; PROTO="${4:-any}"; CHOST="${5:-}"; CPORT="${6:-}"
  [ "$CHOST" = "-" ] && CHOST=""
  [ "$CPORT" = "-" ] && CPORT=""
  command -v tcpdump >/dev/null || { echo "tcpdump is not installed" >&2; exit 1; }
  valid_iface "$IFACE" || { echo "invalid interface" >&2; exit 1; }
  echo "$COUNT" | grep -Eq '^[0-9]{1,3}$' && [ "$COUNT" -ge 1 ] && [ "$COUNT" -le 500 ] || { echo "count must be 1-500" >&2; exit 1; }
  case "$PROTO" in any|tcp|udp|icmp) ;; *) echo "proto must be any|tcp|udp|icmp" >&2; exit 1 ;; esac
  [ -z "$CHOST" ] || valid_ip "$CHOST" || { echo "invalid host (IPv4)" >&2; exit 1; }
  if [ -n "$CPORT" ]; then
    echo "$CPORT" | grep -Eq '^[0-9]{1,5}$' && [ "$CPORT" -ge 1 ] && [ "$CPORT" -le 65535 ] || { echo "invalid port" >&2; exit 1; }
  fi
  set -- -n -p -i "$IFACE" -c "$COUNT" -s 96 -tttt -q -K
  need_and=0
  [ "$PROTO" = any ] || { set -- "$@" "$PROTO"; need_and=1; }
  if [ -n "$CHOST" ]; then [ "$need_and" = 1 ] && set -- "$@" and; set -- "$@" host "$CHOST"; need_and=1; fi
  if [ -n "$CPORT" ]; then [ "$need_and" = 1 ] && set -- "$@" and; set -- "$@" port "$CPORT"; fi
  exec timeout 25 tcpdump "$@"
fi

TOOL="${1:-}"
HOST="${2:-}"
ARG="${3:-}"

valid_host "$HOST" || { echo "invalid host/target" >&2; exit 1; }

case "$TOOL" in
  ping)
    command -v ping >/dev/null || { echo "ping is not installed" >&2; exit 1; }
    if [ -n "$ARG" ]; then
      valid_iface "$ARG" || { echo "invalid interface" >&2; exit 1; }
      timeout 12 ping -c4 -W2 -I "$ARG" "$HOST"
    else
      timeout 12 ping -c4 -W2 "$HOST"
    fi
    ;;
  dns)
    command -v nslookup >/dev/null || { echo "nslookup is not installed" >&2; exit 1; }
    if [ -n "$ARG" ]; then
      valid_ip "$ARG" || { echo "invalid DNS server" >&2; exit 1; }
      timeout 10 nslookup "$HOST" "$ARG"
    else
      timeout 10 nslookup "$HOST"
    fi
    ;;
  trace)
    if command -v traceroute >/dev/null; then
      if [ -n "$ARG" ]; then
        valid_iface "$ARG" || { echo "invalid interface" >&2; exit 1; }
        timeout 30 traceroute -w2 -q1 -i "$ARG" "$HOST"
      else
        timeout 30 traceroute -w2 -q1 "$HOST"
      fi
    elif command -v tracepath >/dev/null; then
      timeout 30 tracepath "$HOST"
    else
      echo "traceroute/tracepath is not installed" >&2
      exit 1
    fi
    ;;
  mtr)
    command -v mtr >/dev/null || { echo "mtr is not installed" >&2; exit 1; }
    if [ -n "$ARG" ]; then
      valid_iface "$ARG" || { echo "invalid interface" >&2; exit 1; }
      timeout 25 mtr --report --report-cycles 5 -I "$ARG" "$HOST"
    else
      timeout 25 mtr --report --report-cycles 5 "$HOST"
    fi
    ;;
  http)
    command -v curl >/dev/null || { echo "curl is not installed" >&2; exit 1; }
    FMT='HTTP %{http_code} | connect %{time_connect}s | total %{time_total}s | peer %{remote_ip}\n'
    if [ -n "$ARG" ]; then
      valid_iface "$ARG" || { echo "invalid interface" >&2; exit 1; }
      timeout 15 curl -sS --interface "$ARG" --max-time 10 -o /dev/null -w "$FMT" "https://$HOST"
    else
      timeout 15 curl -sS --max-time 10 -o /dev/null -w "$FMT" "https://$HOST"
    fi
    ;;
  *)
    echo "usage: saguaro-tools ping|dns|trace|mtr|http HOST [IFACE|SERVER]" >&2
    exit 2
    ;;
esac
